#====================================================================
# Draft: Mailutils on HarmonyOS -- HMDFS UID mapping / hardlink denial
#        plus application UIDs absent from the passwd database
#====================================================================

id:                     E3516
trigger_tool:           mailutils|autotools|conan|make-check
phase:                  runtime|testing|account-lookup

error_signature:        File owner mismatch|link(at)? .*Operation not permitted|cannot determine user name|cannot determine my username|getpw(uid|nam).*NULL|comsat.*passwd

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, ohos, libc, filesystem, passwd-db
match_keywords:         Mailutils, HarmonyOS PC, HMDFS, st_uid, getuid, getpwuid, getpwnam, passwd database, LOGNAME, USER, hardlink, linkat, renameat, EPERM, maildir, File Safety, comsat, test mode

title:                  HarmonyOS HMDFS can expose a mapped file-owner UID and reject hardlinks, while app UIDs may have no passwd record; treat these as separate platform capabilities

root_cause:             On the captured HarmonyOS PC device, getuid() returned 20020085 while stat().st_uid for a newly created HMDFS file returned 20001006. HMDFS also rejected linkat() with EPERM. Separately, the application UID had no traditional passwd database entry, so getpwuid()/getpwnam() could legitimately return NULL. Callers that require st_uid == getuid(), assume linkat() always works, or dereference a NULL passwd result fail for different reasons.

affected_scope:         Autotools packages with file-safety tests, Maildir link-based transitions, or current-user tools and daemons that call getpwuid/getpwnam on HarmonyOS PC. Verified against GNU Mailutils 3.20 upstream make-check logs on device.

verification_cmd:       conan create archives/m/mailutils/3.20 -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64 --build=missing   # inspect all 21 Autotest suite summaries; do not convert failures to skips
rec_priority:           2
rec_approach:            hmdfs-owner-aware-test-fixture-plus-scoped-rename-fallback-and-null-safe-current-user-lookup
rec_description:        (1) Keep production mu_file_safety_check() intact; in the File Safety test helper, use stat().st_uid as the expected file owner when HMDFS reports a mapped UID. A consumer assertion still rejects an explicit foreign UID. (2) For a Maildir temporary-to-destination transition, attempt linkat() and fall back to same-filesystem renameat() only for known unsupported-link errors; propagate other errors. (3) Check passwd lookup results before dereference. Use LOGNAME/USER only as a fallback for the current process identity, limit comsat's user-switch bypass to test mode, and in test mode accept a non-root .biffrc owner when HMDFS maps it. Keep all upstream cases running rather than skipping the platform-sensitive cases.
rec_command:             grep -nE 'st_uid|getuid|linkat|renameat|getpwuid|getpwnam|test_mode' archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0012-*.patch archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0013-*.patch archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0017-*.patch archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0018-*.patch archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0019-*.patch
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0012-mailtools-current-user-fallback.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0013-maildir-linkat-rename-fallback.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0014-testsuite-fsaf-hardlink-fallback.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0016-testsuite-fsaf-hmdfs-owner-mapping.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0017-comsat-test-mode-user-bypass.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0018-testsuite-fsaf-hmdfs-owner-check.patch|archives/m/mailutils/3.20/patches/0019-comsat-test-mode-passwd-guard.patch

fallback_priority:       3
fallback_approach:       preserve-failure-and-report-platform-capability
fallback_description:   If the platform behavior cannot be handled safely, report the unsupported operation or unresolved identity and fail the affected test. Do not synthesize passwd records, silently substitute an arbitrary UID, ignore all link errors, or mark these cases skipped.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:       false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:        fake-passwd-record|global-getpwuid-stub|ignore-all-linkat-errors|skip-file-owner-tests|skip-comsat-tests
forbid_1_reason:         These workarounds hide the HarmonyOS capability boundary or weaken unrelated production checks; they can make a false pass while mailbox delivery, ownership checks, or failure reporting remain broken.
forbid_1_consequence:    Incorrect current-user identity, masked filesystem failures, or a green make-check result that does not exercise the affected paths.

principles:               
# Provenance
# Existing formal entries: E011 (mapped HMDFS owner), E079 (hardlink denial),
# E338 (missing passwd entry). This draft adds the mail-stack interaction and
# scoped current-user/test-mode mitigation; it does not claim the primitives
# are absent from the knowledge base.
source_pr:               15271
source_commit:           69b0bf8c97a75ff9fbbdd4ca4837ce877f49aed4
last_updated:               2026-10-19
authors:               iKalous_OscarP
doc_file:               doc/E3516.md
